+# Dual hunter positions. Measured geometry - hunter spot (0, 16.629, -21), ducks line up at z=104, about 125 m apart.
+#
+# This was re-decided once (2026-08-15).
+#   The first version used ±15 to "guard both flanks and create crossfire", but after a real run **the user judged the fire coverage too oppressive** —
+#   with the two sniper spots 30 m apart, whichever way a duck runs it's in front of one of them, which is too much pressure.
+#   It's now **side by side in the middle**. Each hunter steps one body-width outward from the original spot, shoulder to shoulder guarding the center.
+#   That way their views mostly overlap, fire is concentrated rather than pincering, and ducks still have flanks to go around.
