+# [MP8] ===== Placement-based scoring (T13, finalized by the user 2026-08-15) =====
+#
+# Vanilla is cumulative. A duck reaching the exit gets +1 (the first gets another +1), getting shot is 0, and the hunter gets +1 per kill.
+# The problem is that **a single round can open a gap of at most 2 points, and 3rd and 6th place score exactly the same** —
+# placement information gets squashed and can't shake up the overall standings (see section 6.5 "hard to come back").
+#
+# Now it uses the minigame's **own existing order arrays** as the placement source (players_shot / players_finished),
+# the same approach as the elimination minigames.
+#
+#   Duck · shot       i-th to die            → 2i          (first to die = 0 points)
+#   Duck · escaped    j-th to reach exit     → 2(D-1-j)    (first to arrive = highest score)
+#   Hunters (shared)  score = health knocked off = 2×kills + 1×wounded escapes
+#
+# The two sets of scores fit together into exactly {0,2,4,…,2(D-1)}, with no duplicates or gaps (the dead take the low slots, escapees the high ones).
+#
+# **Why the step is 2 and not 1** - it leaves room to express "wounded = half a duck" as an integer.
+# A duck has 2 health, a body shot does 1 damage and a headshot 2, so using "health" as the unit of score is the most natural.
+# Headshot kill = 2 points, two-body-shot kill = 1+1 = 2 points (**equal to a headshot, inefficient play isn't rewarded**),
+# wounded but escaped = 1 point.
+const MP8_DUCK_RANK_STEP: int = 2
+const MP8_DUCK_MAX_HEALTH: int = 2
+
+# How many ducks this round started with (needed to score "j-th to arrive". duck_player_count gets changed by
+# remove_player_rpc, so a separate snapshot is stored at round start)
+var _mp8_round_duck_count: int = 0
+
+
+# [MP8] How much health has already been knocked off this duck. Used to give hunters half for a "wounded escape".
+# Clamped to [0, max_health]. A dead duck's health can be 0 or negative (a headshot on a wounded duck = overkill damage),
+# and without the clamp overkill damage would add extra points.
+func _mp8_damage_taken(duck) -> int:
+	if duck == null or not is_instance_valid(duck):
+		return 0
+	var max_hp: int = duck.max_health if "max_health" in duck else MP8_DUCK_MAX_HEALTH
+	var hp: int = duck.health if "health" in duck else max_hp
+	return clampi(max_hp - hp, 0, max_hp)
+
+
+# [MP8] Dual hunters **cooperate**. They share a total score, purely ducks vs hunters, with no competition between hunters (one of the four points the user signed off on).
+# So every score event **adds the same points to every hunter**, not just the one who fired.
+# Side effect - a single hunter also goes through this path, and the behavior is identical to vanilla.
+func _mp8_award_hunters(amount: int) -> void :
+	for h in hunter_players:
+		if not is_instance_valid(h):
+			continue
+		if h.player_presence == null:
+			continue
+		var hid: int = h.player_presence.network_id
+		if player_scores.has(hid):
+			player_scores[hid] += amount
+		else:
+			player_scores[hid] = amount
